 3. 📺 GOP convention runs into NFL openers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Republicans will have some stiff competition for eyeballs when they hold their first-ever midterm convention on Sept. 9-10 in Dallas: The NFL, American television's undisputed champion of ratings, will be kicking off Week 1.

 Some GOP operatives are privately incredulous that a convention designed to draw attention to the party's fall candidates was scheduled opposite the NFL, Axios' Alex Isenstadt writes. They fear the GOP will struggle to persuade voters — particularly men, who powered President Trump's 2024 comeback — to choose politics over football. 👀 What to watch: The convention's opening night will overlap with the New England Patriots playing the Seattle Seahawks in a Super Bowl rematch. In Dallas that night, Vice President Vance will deliver the convention's keynote speech.

 The convention's second night will coincide with a rivalry matchup between the San Francisco 49ers and the Los Angeles Rams. Trump is the keynoter that night. 📱 Convention planners tell us they're well aware of the competition from the NFL. But they argue they'd be fighting for eyeballs even without football, given how dramatically Americans' media habits have changed.

 So they're planning a faster-paced, social media-focused convention designed to produce moments that can break through online, whether or not voters are watching live. Social-media influencers will be distributing content on Facebook, X, TikTok and more.

 Organizers plan commemorations to mark the one-year anniversary of pro-Trump activist Charlie Kirk's assassination and the 25th anniversary of the Sept. 11 terror attacks. Entertainers and sports figures, including UFC fighters, will be spotlighted. Share this story . 

 
 
